===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# In a manner without [[pause]] or [[stop]], especially to the point of [[annoyance]]; not [[cease|ceasing]].
#: {{synonyms|en|ceaselessly|continuously|unremittingly|Thesaurus:continuously}}
#: {{ux|en|He jabbered '''incessantly''' and annoyed everyone.}}
#* {{RQ:Landon Ethel Churchill|volume=I|page=136|passage=We see the eye subdued, the practised smile, / The word well weighed before it pass the lip, / And know not of the misery within: / Yet there it works '''incessantly''', and fears / The time to come; for time is terrible, / Avenging, and betraying.}}
#* {{RQ:Thoreau Cape Cod|page=14|passage=There were the tawny rocks, like lions couchant, defying the ocean, whose waves '''incessantly''' dashed against and scoured them with vast quantities of gravel.}}
#* {{RQ:Carroll Alice|page=63|passage="You are old, Father William," the young man said, / "And your hair has become very white; / And yet you '''incessantly''' stand on your head— / Do you think, at your age, it is right?"}}
#* {{RQ:Lindsay Age of Consent|year=1962|page=59|passage=But just there a small hairy terrier exploded out at the gate, like a floor-mop impelled by some sort of internal combustion, which sent him off into a frenzy of yapping, '''incessantly''' jerked backwards by the explosive force of his own detonations.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[immediately|Immediately]].

